s6-3-p12 : Block
s6-3-p12 = prose (cons "**A transformation of an interpreter definition.** For a context \(\Gamma\), the interpreter is the fold of the inductive expression signature" (cons "\[" (cons "\mathsf{Expr}(\Gamma)=\mathsf{var}(\Gamma)+\mathsf{num}(\mathbb N)" (cons " +\mathsf{plus}(\mathsf{Expr}(\Gamma)^2)" (cons " +\mathsf{mul}(\mathsf{Expr}(\Gamma)^2)," (cons "\]" (cons "where the notation describes its four constructor families, not a recursive equation in ordinary sets. The **represented algebra** of clauses over a carrier \(R\) and environment \(\rho:\Gamma\to R\) is the typed record" (cons "\[" (cons "\begin{aligned}" (cons "\mathsf{Clauses}(R):=\;&" (cons "(\Gamma\to R)\times(\mathbb N\to R)\\" (cons "&\times(R\times R\to R)\times(R\times R\to R),\\" (cons "\mathsf{fold}_{R}:\;&\mathsf{Clauses}(R)\to\mathsf{Expr}(\Gamma)\to R." (cons "\end{aligned}" (cons "\tag{6.14}" (cons "\]" (cons "The fold is defined on each constructor by applying the corresponding record component. In the first component the input \(" (cons "\rho:\Gamma\to R\) is part of the record; the second, third, and fourth components interpret constants, addition, and multiplication. For a semiring \(R\), construct the *represented interpreter definition*" (cons "\[" (cons "I_R(\rho):=(\rho,\eta_R,+_R,\cdot_R):\mathsf{Clauses}(R)." (cons "\]" (cons "The construction \((R,\rho)\mapsto I_R(\rho)\), for a specified semiring structure on \(R\), supplies an interpreter definition, not merely an input program. Its meaning is" (cons "\[" (cons "\mathsf{fold}_{R}(I_R(\rho),e)=\llbracket e\rrbracket_R(\rho)," (cons "\]" (cons "proved by the four constructor equations. If \(h:R\to S\) is a semiring homomorphism and \(\rho_S=h\circ\rho_R\), the constructor proof gives" (cons "\[" (cons " h(\mathsf{fold}_{R}(I_R(\rho_R),e))" (cons " =\mathsf{fold}_{S}(I_S(\rho_S),e)." (cons "\]" (cons "The record and its fold are terms available for further computation. Syntactic inspection or rewriting uses their represented code and the quotation/readback conditions of §6.1; the semantic algebra alone does not supply a code representation." nil)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
